{"step_index":11290,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T15:09:14Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-26T15:09:14Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-26T15:09:16Z\nThe search for \"azure linux vm default username home directory azureuser site:learn.microsoft.com\" returned the following summary:\nFor Azure Linux virtual machines, `azureuser` is a common default username often suggested during the creation process, though you can specify a different username if you choose[1][2][3].\n\nThe home directory for this user (or any user created during the VM provisioning process) is located at:\n\n**/home/azureuser**[4][5]\n\n### Key Details:\n*   **Customization:** While `azureuser` is the default recommendation in the Azure portal and CLI documentation, it is not a hard requirement; you can define a different administrative username during VM deployment[1][2].\n*   **Home Directory Path:** Consistent with standard Linux conventions, the home directory for a user named `username` will be `/home/username`[6][4].\n*   **Deletion:** If you use the Azure CLI command `az vm user delete` to remove a user account, the associated home directory on the Linux VM is also deleted[7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFKvhkqqeVnoBZJxW99q_RY5ER2aw7WyuhS8KYP7yWF7s--I9PvOAWhHWa4GuDeayfKZ9CGMILpQnB0YzoH7MNyht0xGz3G0C6PyHvbEqAxJelAJLbNTDa2tDK7w2zSse31Wnm7HqI4sdAHRJWg4r-7liLbBqbyArFN9wS7nGxHC8B0eORvGcQ=)\n[2] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGBE95SYsUgD1ZMi7nIZUMSDoa_rE0XJgwOY6jsJfp7DUWv2Er6rb-68_y_ThEQ1Rqr-ipZ9xwUUpsxWtybmvegeC_Ca7xxUQGQnq5hte3ua4hB2VeqqEfQ-WHGNwjzl6ff05jM_dxcMOyNcJT7U4F6QKvz6ItUh5PcQU_gx1IJuamV6bWdIXcSa0K9fCPYiMynr0-UbX_olKIJgA==)\n[3] [matrixpost.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH7l6SnQsVlHzzTPUbThS9ipeS9jThTLsYHCnT6OQ1Kn0lWISD6ZNnScAZF-TnvWneDjhSyv7tc86xZzz7cuCHWUirEluH8-Lj5O1151ggie6YM0SQh