{"step_index":11291,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T15:09:16Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"domain":"learn.microsoft.com","query":"\"azureuser\" azure vm create default username learn.microsoft.com","toolAction":"Searching Azure VM creation defaults","toolSummary":"Search Azure VM default admin username"}}]}
{"step_index":11292,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T15:09:19Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-26T15:09:19Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-26T15:09:22Z\nThe search for \"\"azureuser\" azure vm create default username learn.microsoft.com\" returned the following summary:\nWhen creating an Azure Virtual Machine, **\"azureuser\"** is a commonly suggested default username in Microsoft Learn documentation and tutorials[1][2][3], but it is **not a system-enforced default**[4].\n\n### Key Points:\n*   **No Automatic Default:** Azure does not automatically assign a \"default\" username to your VM[4]. When you create a VM, you are required to specify an administrator username[2][5]. \n*   **Common Convention:** Because \"azureuser\" is frequently used in Microsoft's own quickstarts and learning paths (such as the Azure Fundamentals exercises)[1][6], many users assume it is the standard default[7][8].\n*   **Reserved Usernames:** While \"azureuser\" is a common suggestion, certain usernames are **disallowed** or reserved by the system (e.g., \"root,\" \"admin,\" \"administrator,\" \"test,\" etc.)[9]. If you attempt to use these, the provisioning process will fail[5][9].\n*   **How to check or change your username:**\n    *   **If you created the VM:** You likely set the username during the creation process (via the Azure Portal, CLI, or Template)[1][2][10].\n    *   **If you forgot the username:** You can reset the credentials for the VM by navigating to the **\"Reset password\"** blade under the **\"Support + troubleshooting\"** section of your VM in the Azure portal[11][12]. This allows you to set a new username and password for the administrative account[12].\n\nSources:\n[1] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGBRT_3EzYcdo4AWH8uSYjLypiU7UTiTD2hTyhO7ZIIWZSO3L48HnGAGDjK_b1rB0Xa46-ivoW4sNDJopehDCkolc9_ZMsC6w3KyOP2bNkMpYjM38f80YU_0AaNVB_7DWK2KdWlpzW66vEZ08l-s6TnD4BIAJ8OHPlMrk091g4FyRQ9IQZlHSs=)